# MadGraph5 batch script: lt~ lt > qt qt~ NP<=1
# in vibegraph_toy_UFO, restricted by restrict_dipole.dat.
#
# Why this exact process:
#   The dipole vertex whose Lorentz structure writes `Sigma` literally --
#   Sigma(3,-1,2,-2)*P(-1,3)*ProjM(-2,1), a momentum-contracted sigma^{mu nu}
#   with a chiral projector. No FeynRules-written model emits the operator that
#   way: FeynRules expands sigma^{mu nu} into gamma^mu gamma^nu before it writes
#   the UFO, so `Sigma` lives in ALOHA's object library and in no model file.
#
#   The dipole and the plain gauge coupling sit on the same qt~ qt vt vertex at
#   different coupling orders, so MadGraph splits them into two interactions and
#   the row is two diagrams sharing one s-channel propagator. The dipole's phase
#   and normalisation are therefore visible in the interference, per helicity,
#   and not only in the helicity sum.
#
# The model path is repo-relative to the vendored UFO; build.sh rewrites it to
# the work-area copy it stages under output/models/. This model is ours, so its
# restrict cards live inside the model directory and are staged with it.
#
# `display interactions` prints the count MadGraph's own interaction splitting
# arrives at (one interaction per coupling-order tuple, import_ufo.add_interaction)
# into the build log, which is where extract_interactions.py reads it from.
#
# The order bound is explicit on every row of this model: an unbounded generate
# runs MadGraph's WEIGHTED search, which would drop the higher-order diagram the
# interference needs.
import model validation/ufo/vibegraph_toy_UFO-dipole
display interactions
generate lt~ lt > qt qt~ NP<=1
output ll_to_qqx_toy_dipole -nojpeg
launch
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set ebeam1 250
set ebeam2 250
set use_syst False
done
